  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello, Im just asking if you guys can work more towards stabilizing / fixing or working more towards fixing basic and some major things for full body tracking. My biggest concern about full body tracking is, you know with htc vive, you have the room setup, were you setup the vive with your surroundings etc and the vive will know where the ground is and all that good stuff, well in vrchat, the ground does not level with the ground i Calibrated in room setup for the htc vive, i dont know if there is a way to fix this in vrchat that is why im coming here because if this is a bug then now you guys know, but yea you know how when you have the 3 vive trackers, 1 on hip and 2 on feet, and in vrchat when you pick an avatar from the menus, you select it then you need to calibrate the character to work with full body tracking, what i mean is you have the white circles, you have to level them right, 1 white circle for your hip, and the 2 other white circles for your feet.. but the two white circles for my feet.. then do not reach my feet, they are always above feet and near knees or below knees a little bit, and you know when you press the menu button on your vive controller, you look down and there is this thin little blue circle around you that should be on the ground, its not on the ground for me, the thin blue circle is in the right place, the thin blue circle is were i calibrated my floor but why isnt my feet there. lol, i dont know, i was hoping this was a bug, if not i really need some help with full body tracking setup for models. ",
